    <GaugingStation location="Beck Bridge" name="Lea Brook" number="33023">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Crump profile weir gauging a rural, Chalk catchment with some Boulder Clay and terrace deposits and with some artificial influences, all but the very highest flows are contained.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">The POR maximum flow is believed to have been in Sept 1968, estimated as 15.1 cumecs by the EA but likely to have been extrapolated.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Crump profile weir 4m wide, situated approx. 20m u/s of new road bridge.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2020 (WINFAP Files v9).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Some groundwater abstraction for PWS, also industrial/agricultural abstraction. Runoff increased by effluent returns.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">A rural Chalk catchment with Boulder Clay cover in upper (S) part of catchment. Some river terrace deposits in N. Mixed agricultural land use.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">GEI</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Although not gauged to within 30% of QMED, theoretical rating expected to perform well to QMED." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Few high flow gaugings. Rating can not be validated beyond QMED." suitable="No" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
